# fixedbugs, defect 2364, lane p239-land-a, 2026-11-09, a shape beside the
# repair's own route.
#
# This unit reads `fixedbugs-2364-rs.h` before `fixedbugs-2364-wide.h`, the
# order under which `Rs` reads as module `rs` reads it, and spells `hd.Hd`
# too, a handle whose header no record is read from. The sitting's prototype
# composed the list from the records' headers alone, so `fixedbugs-2364-hd.h`
# was dropped and this correct program was refused, *`hd.h` declares no
# `Hd`*. A header of the list that no reordered block holds follows them, as
# it stood.
use fixedbugs2364/defines_wide
use fixedbugs2364/hd
use fixedbugs2364/rs

function main()
    h = hd.none()
    p = defines_wide.make(v: 4)
    r = rs.make(v: 3)
    print(p.w + r.a + r.b)
    print(hd.is_none(h: h))
